
Example mesh scan: 
    
    RE(mesh(huber.x, -0.4, -0.3026, 10, huber.z, 0.84, 0.94198, 10, 1, att_ratio=1))

to view the mesh, run the following command in your ipython console, passing the uid and signal ROI: 

    plot_mesh("9d8219bc-3ce4-4012-b25c-743b6f0e354f", signal="lambda2M_stats2_total")


one axis linear scans: 

scan eta: 
RE(dscan(huber.eta, -.5, .5, 40, 0.1, lambda2M, att_ratio=10))

scan y:
RE(dscan(huber.y, -.5, .5, 40, 0.1, lambda2M, att_ratio=10))

cahkl(1.5, 0.5, 8)
psic.move(h, k, l)


